ppwriteCountIsAnAddress -- chainTruthT'S OUTPUT DIFFERS BETWEEN IDENTICAL RUNS, AND THE CAUSE IS AN INSTRUMENT.

Found 2026-09-29 bisecting the R2 try-and-buy (recon 19): three identical chainTruthT runs gave three different md5s, so
an output compare could not be used on it (it was bisected by exit status instead). Two runs, addresses masked, differ in
exactly two lines, both PPWRITE:
    PPWRITE tag=grup field= body= data=6 count=9695744  ...
    PPWRITE tag=grup field= body= data=6 count=12235264 ...
measurePlusPlusWrite (measure.twk) prints `count=%d` from groupBody->gCount UNCONDITIONALLY. When the field's data is a
GROUP (data=6) that union slot holds a pointer, so the "count" is the pointer's low bits -- it moves with ASLR, and the
0x-masking every harness applies cannot see it because it is printed as a decimal.

No fleet row reads it today (chainTruthT's rows assert other lines), so nothing is red. It costs an instrument: any
output-compare of a traced run that crosses a ++ on a group-holding field is nondeterministic.

Run this file twice and compare the PPWRITE count= values: they differ.

NEXT: BEST GUESS -- print count only when the data is a count (isCOUNT), and otherwise print `count=-` (or the group's tag).
